    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d525">

                <pb facs="0597" n="585" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg585"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.00/1788: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Finland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gullion</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Helsinki</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-30T18:00:00+02:00">March 30, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:01 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>292. Department of State memorandum on foreign policy of March 21<anchor n="97"
                        xml:id="d525-f1"/> seems not to have been reported except in few lines by
                        FNB<anchor n="98" xml:id="d525-f2"/> from United States of America and was
                    hardly noted in press.</p>
                <p>Procopé has referred to memorandum in his cables and there is tendency here to be
                    encouraged by references to rights of small nations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gullion</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d525-f1" n="97" xml:id="d525-f1-content">
                <p>The Department released to the press on March 21, 1944, a memorandum entitled,
                    “Bases of the Foreign Policy of the United States”; see Department of State <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, March 25, 1944, p. 275.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d525-f2" n="98" xml:id="d525-f2-content">
                <p>Finska Nyhets Byrån, Finnish News Bureau.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
